Package: citelens
Type: Package
Title: Tools for Citation Libraries and Text Analytics on Abstracts
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Mario", "Martinez", email = "mario.a.martinez@live.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Converts 'RefWorks' and 'RIS' exports, and saved 'Google Scholar'
    results pages, to 'BibTeX', and reads 'BibTeX' files into data frames and
    'Excel' workbooks. Looks up missing abstracts in 'OpenAlex'. Runs text
    analytics on abstracts: topic modeling (latent Dirichlet allocation),
    cosine document similarity, and trends over time. The computationally heavy
    steps are implemented in 'C++' via 'Rcpp'.
URL: https://github.com/cownr10r/citelens
BugReports: https://github.com/cownr10r/citelens/issues
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: Rcpp, writexl, ggplot2, xml2, jsonlite, curl
LinkingTo: Rcpp
Suggests: readxl, testthat (>= 3.0.0), withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
